+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out of Scope, Specialty Filtering Does Not
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined search for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners the only searchable entity. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so whether it was a decision or a gap stayed open.
+
+A request arrived on 2026-08-15 to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty. The row as written could be read either way: a specialty filter is not free-text search, but it is a way of finding veterinarians. [The 2026-08-08 non-goal ADR](2026-08-08-non-goal-deletion-and-visit-amendment.md) had already fixed the convention — a request never reopens a row by implication, only a recorded owner decision does.
+
+The owner decided the row at intake (2026-08-15).
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Hold NG-9 whole.** Decline the filter as veterinarian search. Rejected by the owner: the directory already displays the specialties, so narrowing by one adds no new information surface.
+2. **Retire NG-9.** Open veterinarian search generally. Rejected: free-text search over veterinarians would repeat what owner search already demonstrates, which is the row's standing reason.
+3. **Narrow NG-9 to free-text search** (chosen).
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 covers free-text search only. Narrowing a listing by an attribute that listing already shows is in scope, and `REQ-VET-003` is the first such capability. Pet and visit search remain declined in full, and free-text veterinarian search remains declined.
+
+The row keeps its original rationale: owner search demonstrates paged prefix search once. Filtering a displayed attribute is a different capability from searching, so the rationale is untouched by the narrowing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- NG-9 leaves the open provenance consultation; it is decided as narrowed rather than confirmed whole.
+- Narrowing another listing by a displayed attribute now has a precedent, but still needs its own recorded owner decision.
+- `REQ-VET-002` was withdrawn as an unrequested artifact; the same intake reinstated that surface as `REQ-VET-004`, so both directory forms carry the filter.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row.
+- [PRD REQ-VET-003](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the capability the narrowing admits.
